# `lti::PoleZero::is_cont`

[Back to `lti::PoleZero`](../PoleZero.md)

Whether the system is continuous-time (sample time zero).

## Signature

```cpp
bool lti::PoleZero::is_cont() const noexcept;
```

## What It Does

True when `sample_time()` is zero. Use it to decide how to read the poles and zeros: in the `s` plane for a continuous system. It is the negation of [`is_disc`](is_disc.md).

## Returns

`true` for a continuous-time system, `false` otherwise.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The default is continuous.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace lti = pluss::subsp::eng::lti;
using namespace pluss::tils;

// G(s) = 5 (s + 1) / ((s + 2)(s + 3))
static lti::PoleZero plant(double sample_time = 0.0) { return lti::zpk(pluss::make_series({-1.0}), pluss::make_series({-2.0, -3.0}), pluss::make_series(5.0), sample_time); }

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  out.writeln("continuous:", plant().is_cont());
}
```

### Example 2

A sample time makes it discrete.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace lti = pluss::subsp::eng::lti;
using namespace pluss::tils;

// G(s) = 5 (s + 1) / ((s + 2)(s + 3))
static lti::PoleZero plant(double sample_time = 0.0) { return lti::zpk(pluss::make_series({-1.0}), pluss::make_series({-2.0, -3.0}), pluss::make_series(5.0), sample_time); }

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  out.writeln("continuous:", plant(0.1).is_cont());
}
```

### Example 3

A digital filter from `signal::butter` is discrete.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace lti = pluss::subsp::eng::lti;
using namespace pluss::tils;

// G(s) = 5 (s + 1) / ((s + 2)(s + 3))
static lti::PoleZero plant(double sample_time = 0.0) { return lti::zpk(pluss::make_series({-1.0}), pluss::make_series({-2.0, -3.0}), pluss::make_series(5.0), sample_time); }

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  namespace sig = pluss::subsp::eng::signal;
  out.writeln("continuous:", sig::butter(2, 0.3).is_cont());
}
```

